WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:14,020
What is the difference between tumor cells and cancer cells? Is there a difference?

00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:20,020
You've touched on this on many, many Zoom calls. There really is no difference.

00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:28,020
It's old terminology. What's a tumor? What's a cancerous tumor? What's just cancer? How's there a difference?

00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:40,020
It's hard when there's been decades and decades of medicine and terminology used in the practice of medicine.

00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:51,020
And updated terminology is still used, but then the old terminology is used everywhere. It's interchangeable.

00:00:51,020 --> 00:01:00,020
So, or is a tumor benign, or is it malignant? Well, it depends on what adjective you put in front of it.

00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:10,020
So, when you say cancer, then you always know that's a malignant disease. If you say tumor, then you have to know what adjective you put in front of it.

00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:15,020
Is it a malignant tumor? Is it benign tumor? It's semantics.

00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:24,330
People who say stay away from animal protein, can they use collagen? Maybe, maybe not.

00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:30,330
So, we test for that if we think the person should be able to use collagen or not.

00:01:30,330 --> 00:01:35,330
If you're a hardcore vegan, then you're not taking collagen.

00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:44,330
But if you're only taking away from animal protein because you have cancer and animal protein can feed the cancer, then typically not.

00:01:44,330 --> 00:02:02,330
You could use collagen. But if you're stayed away from animal protein for some moral ethical reason, then you would probably stay away from collagen as well.

00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:06,330
So, cancer, no, you're probably safe with collagen.

